    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d749">

                <pb facs="0816" n="806" xml:id="pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.61/972: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-18">January 18,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received January 19—1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. Stettinius’<anchor n="22" xml:id="d749-f1"/> radio statement regarding
                    United States cooperation with Soviet Union receives 3½ inches of prominently
                    placed space in Moscow newspapers for January 18.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d749-f2"
                    /> Reporting Under Secretary’s statement that any other policy would be a tragic
                    mistake, item quotes his remarks regarding impression of Soviet peoples
                    resourcefulness and courage derived from contacts with Soviet representatives in
                    America, and statement America has much to gain and nothing to lose by
                    continuing close collaboration with Soviet Union now and after war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d749-f1" n="22" xml:id="d749-f1-content">
                <p>Edward R. Stettinius, Jr., Under Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d749-f2" n="23" xml:id="d749-f2-content">
                <p>These remarks were made during the second broadcast of the National Broadcasting
                    Company series, “The State Department Speaks”; see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, January 15, 1944, p. 74.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
